worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_12.js"
  ceiling 1251
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver: issue #658 divided one oversized worker file by line count, so this shard has no subject of its own. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into src/web/wasm-worker. The +18 lines over the previous 1198 ceiling are pure catalog data, not logic: hive-mind#2158 dispatched Hello World issues in Scala and Kotlin that no catalog language could answer, so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained scala and kotlin in Rust and this mirror gained the matching WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus their two hello_world templates. Mirroring only hello_world follows the existing sparse-coverage precedent (count_to_three carries 6 of 12 languages) and keeps every consumer of WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES consistent; the remaining task templates degrade through the blueprint and oracle fallbacks. The next +19 lines are the same kind of growth for the same reason: issue #1021 asked that a Russian request for PHP code (issue #723) be answered by generalization rather than by a rule written for its wording, and the generalization is cataloguing PHP the way Kotlin was catalogued -- so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained php in Rust and this mirror gained its WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus a php template in each of the task tables it already carries. Data, not logic: the mirror learned no new rule, only one more column of the table it already had. The next +16 lines are catalog data of the same kind, for the reason the PHP row did not settle: answering a request for Laravel in PHP answers the language the framework is written in, not the thing that was asked for (issue #723). The generalization widens the axis rather than adding a rule -- a row is an implementation target and a target may be a framework of another target -- so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained a laravel row in Rust and this mirror gained the matching WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus its hello_world template. Without the mirror the browser engine would answer a bare Laravel request with nothing at all, because the surface moved out of the php meaning and into its own: the +16 lines are what keeps the mirror from regressing while the Rust engine improves. This data moves to src/web/wasm-worker with the rest of the write-program surface."
